Vulkan: flash attention keeps its output accumulator in f32 when F32 precision is asked for.

The FA shaders accumulate the unnormalised sum of P*V in O_TYPE, which was FLOAT_TYPE: f16 in the fp16 build, even in
the variant chosen for GGML_PREC_F32 (that flag only widened the scores and row sums). With attention spread evenly over a
long KV the sum reaches about n_kv * |mean(V)| and overflows 65504 to inf; the result is clamped to +-65504. LTX-2.5's
video-to-audio cross-attention (268 audio queries over 38,808 video tokens at 257 frames, 1344x896) hit it and the refine
pass came out as mush (fornax#112). O_TYPE now follows ACC_TYPE (f16 only when f16 accumulation is allowed), on the
scalar, coopmat1 and coopmat2 paths; the shared-memory estimates count the wider accumulator. Upstream
ggml-org/llama.cpp master (2026-11-28) still has the f16 accumulator; not yet reported there. Drop this once the pinned
engines have a fix.

